// =============================================================================
// Djaber AI v2 — Prisma schema DRAFT (PostgreSQL 16)
// Source of truth: docs/specs/05-data-model.md (§1–§10 + Figma additions §11–§20)
// Status: DRAFT for review — not yet migrated. Generated 2026-10-06.
//
// ASSUMPTIONS (read before editing)
// 1. Ids are UUID v7 generated by the application (`@default(dbgenerated("uuid_generate_v7()"))`
//    requires the pg_uuidv7 extension; replace by `uuid()` if the extension is unavailable).
// 2. Money is Int (DZD, integer dinars). Credits are Int. Percentages are Int (0–100) unless noted.
// 3. Secrets are `Bytes` (AES-256-GCM ciphertext). Tokens/keys are SHA-256 hashes in `String`.
// 4. Every merchant table has `workspaceId` NOT NULL and the workspace FK is `onDelete: Cascade`
//    (hard purge 30 d after soft deletion, D31). Platform tables have no workspaceId.
// 5. Soft delete = `deletedAt DateTime?`. Partial unique indexes ("live rows only", e.g. Product.sku,
//    Client.phone, Membership owner, Subscription current, Shipment active, CustomerBlock active)
//    cannot be expressed in Prisma: they are listed in the `// PARTIAL UNIQUE` comments and must be
//    added in a raw SQL migration. Same for trigram indexes (pg_trgm) on Product search.
// 6. Enum values are snake_case to match the API (JSON) values 1:1.
// 7. Every table of this file is DECIDED (docs/specs/README.md, decisions closed 2026-10-11). Nothing here is
//    conditional on a pending decision.
// 8. Agent wizard fields (05 §15, D54) are columns on `Agent`; they are compiled into `customInstructions` /
//    `humanHandoffRules` at every save (D23 amended).
// 9. `Json` columns hold localized text as `{ "fr": "...", "ar": "...", "en": "..." }`.
// 10. Relation names are explicit wherever a model references User/Workspace more than once.
// =============================================================================

generator client {
  provider        = "prisma-client-js"
  previewFeatures = ["postgresqlExtensions"]
}

datasource db {
  provider   = "postgresql"
  url        = env("DATABASE_URL")
  extensions = [pg_trgm, pgcrypto]
}

